The engine forbids unsafe code, but this optional safe-public-API boundary
includes dependency-internal unsafe representation casts, array/storage
operations and numeric invariants. Disabling tiny-skia SIMD does not make the
dependency tree unsafe-free. No native production backend or PNG feature is
included. Source-derived preflight bounds numerical/work conditions; backend
internal allocations can still abort on genuine process OOM. See
RASTER-DESIGN.md and reference/raster-allocation-audit-r0.json.

